  {
    "id": "7ad160f719253ea8c52c4ef5",
    "path": "parquet::column::page::PageReader::at_record_boundary",
    "name": "at_record_boundary",
    "owner": "parquet::column::page::PageReader",
    "crate": "parquet",
    "version": "59.3.0",
    "kind": "function",
    "signature": "fn at_record_boundary(&mut self) -> Result<bool>",
    "docs": "Returns `true` if the next page can be assumed to contain the start of a new record\n\nPrior to parquet V2 the specification was ambiguous as to whether a single record\ncould be split across multiple pages, and prior to [(#4327)] the Rust writer would do\nthis in certain situations. However, correctly interpreting the offset index relies on\nthis assumption holding [(#4943)], and so this mechanism is provided for a [`PageReader`]\nto signal this to the calling context\n\n[(#4327)]: https://github.com/apache/arrow-rs/pull/4327\n[(#4943)]: https://github.com/apache/arrow-rs/pull/4943",
